# Multi-Environment Deployment & PR Workflow Plan (v2)

Based on your feedback, I've updated the plan to include identified environment badges in the UI and a structured branching strategy.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Environment Badges:** I will implement a badge in the top-right corner that updates based on the current environment:
> - **DEV:** Yellow (Local)
> - **TEST:** Red (DeanOS @ 9700)
> - **PROD:** Green (DeanOS @ 9600)

## Proposed Changes

### [NEW] Environment Files
- `.env.dev`: `APP_ENV=DEV`, `PORT=9600` (Local conflict check).
- `.env.test`: `APP_ENV=TEST`, `PORT=9700`.
- `.env.prod`: `APP_ENV=PROD`, `PORT=9600`.

### [MODIFY] [base.html](file:///c:/projects/it-inventory/templates/base.html)
- Update the bottom environment badge colors:
  - `PROD` -> Green (#10b981)
  - `TEST` -> Red (#ef4444)
  - `DEV` -> Yellow (#f59e0b)

### [MODIFY] [deploy.ps1](file:///c:/projects/it-inventory/deploy.ps1)
- Refactor to handle the "PR Merge" logic:
  - If on `dev`: Commit & push to `origin dev`. (Local restart).
  - If on `test`: Merge from `dev`, push to `origin test`, trigger **DeanOS TEST** update.
  - If on `main`: Merge from `test`, push to `origin main`, trigger **DeanOS PROD** update.

### [NEW] [deploy_deanos.sh](file:///c:/projects/it-inventory/deploy_deanos.sh)
- A server-side script identifying which container to update based on the branch.
- Standardizes command to `sudo HOME=$PWD docker compose up -d --build`.

